<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
    "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        Auspex runs unsandboxed on purpose.

        Its whole job is to observe agent harnesses that write their
        session stores wherever they like: ~/.claude/projects,
        ~/.codex/sessions, ~/.cursor/chats, ~/.grok/sessions, and
        AntiGravity's conversation databases. A sandboxed app cannot
        read across those trees, and it cannot bind the Unix socket at
        ~/.auspex/mcp.sock that the MCP bridge connects to. So
        `com.apple.security.app-sandbox` is intentionally absent.

        Unsandboxed is not a license for casual filesystem access. See
        AGENTS.md § Privacy: read only the harness stores Auspex
        actually observes, treat every one of them as read-only, and
        write nothing outside ~/.auspex/.
    -->
</dict>
</plist>
